    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1979-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each numerator is one more than its denominator, so the expression is \\[ \\begin{aligned} 6+\\biggl(&\\frac12+\\frac14+\\frac18\\\\ &+\\frac1{16}+\\frac1{32}+\\frac1{64}\\biggr)-7. \\end{aligned} \\] The parenthesized geometric sum is \\(1-\\frac{1}{64}=\\frac{63}{64}.\\) Therefore the value is \\(6+\\frac{63}{64}-7=-\\frac{1}{64}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write each fraction as \\(1\\) plus a reciprocal power of \\(2\\)",
        "Sum \\(\\frac12+\\frac14+\\cdots+\\frac1{64}\\) as a finite geometric series"
      ],
